  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 1210.4 K, melting point of Ge; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 8.830$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{0} = 8.204 + 0.492 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.898 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{\\circ}-H_{2,9,8}^{\\circ}=8.204\\times10^{-3}T+0.246\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.898\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.769$ \nFormation equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1210.4 K: $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = -8.304 - 0.992 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.471 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 42.300 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = -8.304 + 0.992 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T + 0.471 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 21.150 T^{-1} - 28.240 \\times 10^{-3} T$ \n1210.4-2000 K: $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = -16.604 - 2.011 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.005 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 67.200 T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = -16.604 + 2.011 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T + 0.005 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 33.600 T^{-1} - 28.061 \\times 10^{-3} T$ \nSource: Data from Pedley (396). ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "Phase change: 1210.4 K, melting point of Ge; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 8.830$ kcal/mol.",
